verses.text:
The lion has roared;
who will not fear?
The Lord Yahweh has spoken;
who will not prophesy?

Therefore, thus I will do to you, Israel;
for the reason that I will do this to you,
prepare to meet your God, Israel!

and do not seek Bethel,
and do not go to Gilgal,
and do not cross over to Beersheba;
for Gilgal, going into exile, will go into exile,
and Bethel will become iniquity.”

The maker of the Pleiades and Orion,
turning deep darkness into morning;
he darkens day into night;
calling for the waters of the sea,
he pours them out on the face of the earth—
Yahweh is his name—

And he said, “What are you seeing, Amos?” And I said, “A basket of summer fruit.” And Yahweh said to me,
“The end has come to my people Israel;
I will not repeat again to pass over him.

And the songs of the temple will wail in that day”—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh—
“many are the corpses;
in every place one has thrown them. Hush!”
